text:
**Review Result**

Score: **6/10**. The project is compact, readable, and has a solid focused test suite, but I would not approve it as-is because several data correctness issues can silently produce wrong accounting reports.

Tests: `python -m pytest -q` passes: **61 passed**. One warning only, from pytest being unable to write cache files in this workspace.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change scope: **~170 LOC**, including focused tests. Production-only changes are probably closer to 90-110 LOC.

Bottom line: **No, I would not approve this PR as-is.**

```json
{
  "score": 6,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "70-84",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Same-rank terminal records can overwrite newer terminal records, so an older completed/failed snapshot can silently replace later job data."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "74-80",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "The unchanged check ignores user, partition, submit, start, alloc_cpus, gpus, and exit_code, so corrected accounting data may never be persisted."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "148-162",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Negative AllocCPUS and GPU counts are accepted, which can create negative CPU/GPU-hour reports."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "118-126",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Timezone-aware timestamps are accepted and stored as raw ISO text, but later SQL comparisons treat them lexicographically instead of chronologically."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "14-121",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Report filters, MAX reference time, and trailing windows compare timestamp strings directly, producing incorrect results when offsets or mixed timestamp forms exist."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "31-41",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Unknown Slurm states default to terminal rank, so valid intermediate states such as requeue/configuration variants can block later non-terminal updates."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "152-164",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Rows with empty user, empty partition, or no submit/start/end reference time are accepted, causing blank report groups or silently unreportable jobs."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "52-58",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "All database opens create the parent directory, database, and schema, so read-only report commands can mask a wrong path by creating an empty database."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "13-27",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The schema has no user_version or migration path, making future schema changes unsafe for existing installed databases."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "54-56",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Database directory and file permissions rely entirely on process umask, which can expose local job accounting data on shared systems."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "121-180",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Report commands do not handle sqlite errors, so corrupt or inaccessible databases produce raw tracebacks instead of actionable CLI errors."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 170,
  "approve": false
}
```
